second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Where is Franklin County High School located?\", \"slot_hint\": \"place\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 208, \"text\": \"Franklin County High School (Kentucky) Franklin County High School is the largest of three public high schools in Frankfort, Kentucky and is one of two high schools operated by Franklin County Public Schools.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d00\", \"start\": 209, \"end\": 312, \"text\": \"The campus also houses the Franklin County Career & Technical Center, which offers vocational training.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d00\", \"start\": 313, \"end\": 366, \"text\": \"The principal of the school is Charles \\\"Chuck\\\" Lewis.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d00\", \"start\": 367, \"end\": 461, \"text\": \"Franklin County High was opened in the fall of 1958 and dedicated on November 30 of that year.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d00\", \"start\": 462, \"end\": 549, \"text\": \"It consolidated Elkhorn, Bridgeport, Bald Knob, Thornhill, and Peaks Mill High Schools.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d00\", \"start\": 550, \"end\": 631, \"text\": \"Franklin County is named for Benjamin Franklin, and the high school's mascot, the\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 210, \"text\": \"Franklin County High School (Illinois) Franklin County High School is the largest of three public high schools in Springfield, Illinois and is one of two high schools operated by Franklin County Public Schools.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d01\", \"start\": 211, \"end\": 314, \"text\": \"The campus also houses the Franklin County Career & Technical Center, which offers vocational training.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d01\", \"start\": 315, \"end\": 368, \"text\": \"The principal of the school is Charles \\\"Chuck\\\" Lewis.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d01\", \"start\": 369, \"end\": 463, \"text\": \"Franklin County High was opened in the fall of 1958 and dedicated on November 30 of that year.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d01\", \"start\": 464, \"end\": 551, \"text\": \"It consolidated Elkhorn, Bridgeport, Bald Knob, Thornhill, and Peaks Mill High Schools.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d01\", \"start\": 552, \"end\": 636, \"text\": \"Franklin County is named for Benjamin Franklin, and the high school's mascot, the...\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 116, \"text\": \"Franklin County High School (Rocky Mount, Virginia) Franklin County High School is located in Rocky Mount, Virginia.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d02\", \"start\": 117, \"end\": 207, \"text\": \"Approximately 2300 students attend Franklin County High School, which was founded in 1950.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d02\", \"start\": 208, \"end\": 343, \"text\": \"Since its founding, Franklin County High School, commonly known as FCHS, has grown to the largest school in the state west of Richmond.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0267-f1163e2d0465:d02\", \"start\": 344, \"end\": 504, \"text\": \"As of the 2015-16 